      "writtenOn": "2021-08-30T15:30:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s written in C, but this change compiles it with the C++ compiler. C++ is backwards compatible with C, so valid C code compiles with a C++ compiler, but the reverse is not true.\n\nIn order to be able to use the C++ classes that libec provides, ectool has to be compiled with C++. See https://crrev.com/c/2556758/22/util/ectool.cc as an example that uses libec\u0027s VersionCommand to replace EC_CMD_GET_CMD_VERSIONS.",
